Subject: [PATCH] vayu data2: IPA pipe-count preflight, uC state at three points, INIT after INDICATION_REGISTER + probe + retries

Base: /mnt/ramdisk/ds-data with 0044 applied (vayu-test26 d15caf0 + 0044). Applies with -p1.
Kernel: mach-data3.bin sha256 f465e26c94ee29f65b50657d31e1fe01ea7b15e66f36c39b46ad27740fbc255b.

Run 115037 facts this patch answers:
- S2 INIT_MODEM_DRIVER TIMEOUT 20000 ms while the request went to service 0x31 v1 inst 2,
  node 0 port 31, message 0x0021; every TLV matches ipa_qmi_service_v01.c
  (ipa3_init_modem_driver_req_msg_data_v01_ei) and the values match vendor ipa_4_1_mem_part
  (ipa_utils.c:3189): hdr 0x688/0x140, v4 rt 0x508 idx 7, v6 0x608, flt 0x308/0x408,
  modem 0x13f0/0x100c, ctrl ep 11, proc 0x7d0/0x200, hash 0x488/0x588/0x288/0x388,
  quota 0xc30/0x60, drop 0x13d0/0x20. The port, instance, message id and TLVs are therefore
  not the fault; the modem never answered (and the 0x24 indication at 208.3 s arrived 5 s
  after the timeout, so the client port is reachable).
- uC NOT READY 8 s after AUTH (responseOp 0x2c, params 0xd041cb06, hwState 0x3f, iface 0x390).
  Stock loads no separate ipa_uc PAS on this phone: vayu's live DT has only qcom,ipa_fws
  (pas-id 0xf) and no qcom,platform-type, and ipa.c only PIL-loads IPA_UC_SUBSYSTEM_NAME when
  platform_type == IPA_PLAT_TYPE_APQ (ipa.c:6649). ipa_uc.mdt is present in /vendor/firmware but
  is not referenced by the DT. What stock does after AUTH is ipa3_post_init: ipa3_init_hw
  (CLKON/QSB/BCR/COMP, ipa_utils.c:4165) and then ipa3_uc_interface_init (map SRAM + IRQ only,
  ipa_uc.c:785; no firmware start). So the previous look 8 s after AUTH, before any CLKON write,
  was not conclusive: this patch reads the uC after AUTH, after the hardware init, after MPSS
  and at every INIT attempt.
- The GSI preflight refused a healthy IPA: IPA_ENABLED_PIPES is a COUNT (stock
  ipa3_get_num_pipes() returns it as is, ipa_utils.c:7075; run 115037 read 0x17 = 23 pipes),
  not a bitmask of endpoint numbers. The old test demanded bits 2/5/10/11 and failed S2.

What:
1. vayu_ipa_data.c: preflight accepts GSI enabled, >=4 event rings and >11 pipes; logs the count.
2. vayu_ipa.c: vayu_ipa_uc_look(when, ms) reads the uC shared area (responseOp/params/hwState/
   interface, polls up to ms) and is called after AUTH ("post-auth"), after the hardware init
   ("post-init", logged as vayu-data: S0 IPA UC OK|ERROR), after MPSS ("after-mpss") and from
   the QMI stage.
3. vayu_ipa_qmi.c: after publishing 0x31/1 it waits for the modem's INDICATION_REGISTER (5 s)
   before the first INIT, sends an unknown-message probe 0x7fff (1 s, tells whether the modem's
   service loop runs at all), then up to 3 INIT_MODEM_DRIVER attempts (timeout each, 1 s apart).
   vayu_ipa_qmi_regwait=MS, vayu_ipa_qmi_attempts=N (1..5). INIT is an init message, not the
   non-idempotent WDS Start, so retrying it is safe. Four more attempts follow one per 30 s
   ("S2 LATE INIT n/4") in case the modem/uC only becomes ready later in the boot.
4. hakios.qmi.c/.h: vayu_qmi_trace=1 traces every datagram on the IPA handle (type, id, message,
   source node/port, first 8 bytes) and a late reply to a given-up transaction; the "nobody
   handles" line now names the source. This settles whether a reply arrives at all and from where.
5. No change for the network: 115037 registered UMTS (MegaFon) at 274 s; the long SEARCHING was
   the modem's scan, not a NAS failure, and nothing in the IPA path touches NAS.

Expected next-run lines:
  vayu-ipa-data: GSI status 0x1 ... IPA has 23 pipes
  vayu-ipa: post-init: uC responseOp ...: uC INIT_COMPLETED | NOT READY
  vayu-data: S0 IPA UC: OK | ERROR
  vayu-ipa-qmi: S2 INDICATION_REGISTER: OK after N ms
  vayu-ipa-qmi: S2 PROBE 0x7fff: OK the service answered ... | TIMEOUT
  vayu-ipa-qmi: S2 INIT_MODEM_DRIVER: attempt 1/3 ...
  vayu-ipa-qmi: S2 INIT_MODEM_DRIVER: OK after N ms ...
  qmi: trace: ... (with vayu_qmi_trace=1)
